-- Q914: Passive Activity and At-Risk Rules [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Gifting the interest to his daughter is the best strategy because suspended losses transfer to the donee and become immediately deductible on her return","Selling 60% of the interest is optimal because it releases a proportional $108,000 of suspended losses while preserving the remaining 40% for future passive income offset","Selling the entire interest to an unrelated buyer is the best strategy because a fully taxable disposition releases all $180,000 of suspended passive losses in the current year","Retaining the interest is preferable because Mercer can offset suspended losses against future passive income without triggering the $50,000 built-in loss on the sale"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 469(g)(1), a fully taxable disposition of an entire passive activity interest to an unrelated party releases all suspended passive losses for deduction against nonpassive income. Selling 100% releases all $180,000, and the $50,000 built-in loss ($200,000 FMV minus $250,000 basis) provides additional capital loss.
Wrong (A): Under Section 469(j)(6), a gift does not release suspended losses for deduction; instead, the losses increase the donee''s basis in the property.
Wrong (B): A partial sale of 60% releases only $108,000 proportionally, leaving $72,000 still suspended.
Wrong (D): Retaining the interest defers the losses indefinitely and relies on uncertain future passive income.$EXPL$
