-- Q922: Passive Activity and At-Risk Rules [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The suspended losses transfer to the daughter and she may deduct them against her own passive income","The donor deducts the $30,000 of suspended losses on her current-year return as a disposition","The basis of the gifted property is increased by $30,000 to $80,000, and no current deduction arises","The suspended losses are permanently disallowed and cannot benefit either the donor or the donee"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 469(j)(6), when a passive activity interest is transferred by gift, suspended losses are not deductible by either party. Instead, the $30,000 of suspended losses increases the donor''s basis to $80,000 ($50,000 + $30,000), which becomes the donee''s carryover basis under Sec. 1015.
Wrong (A): Suspended losses do not transfer to the donee for deduction; they are absorbed into basis under Sec. 469(j)(6).
Wrong (B): A gift is not a fully taxable disposition under Sec. 469(g), so suspended losses are not released for current deduction.
Wrong (D): The losses are not permanently lost; they are preserved through the increased basis, reducing future gain on disposition.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 922;

