UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Separate returns are preferable because each subsidiary can independently optimize deductions and credits without complex consolidated return regulations","The consolidated return is preferable because Subsidiary B''s loss offsets A''s income and the intercompany inventory gain is deferred, reducing current taxable income to $1,600,000","Consolidated returns never provide a benefit here because the SRLY rules prevent Subsidiary B''s losses from offsetting Subsidiary A''s income","The results are identical because intercompany transactions are eliminated under both consolidated and separate return filing methods"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treas. Reg. Sections 1.1502-11 and 1.1502-13, filing consolidated allows B''s $1,200,000 loss to offset A''s income, and the $200,000 intercompany inventory gain is deferred until the property leaves the group. Consolidated taxable income is $1,600,000 ($3,000,000 - $1,200,000 - $200,000), saving approximately $336,000 in current tax versus separate filing.
Wrong (A): Separate filing means B''s loss only creates an NOL carryforward with no current benefit, and the intercompany gain is immediately recognized.
Wrong (C): The SRLY rules limit pre-acquisition losses, not current-year losses generated after the group is formed.
