-- Q972: International Tax [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The payment is made to a domestic corporation rather than a foreign entity","The payment creates a hybrid mismatch that is deductible by the payor but excluded from the payee''s income","The payment exceeds the $1,000,000 threshold for related-party royalty transactions","The payment is for tangible inventory rather than intangible property or services"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 267A, deductions are disallowed for interest or royalty payments that produce a hybrid mismatch outcome, meaning the amount is deductible in the U.S. but not included in the income of the related foreign payee due to differences in entity classification or instrument treatment.
Wrong (A): Payments to domestic corporations do not trigger Section 267A, which targets cross-border hybrid arrangements with foreign related parties.
Wrong (C): Section 267A has no dollar threshold; it applies based on the hybrid mismatch outcome regardless of the payment amount.
Wrong (D): The nature of the payment as inventory versus intangible is not the operative test; Section 267A focuses on deduction/inclusion mismatches.$EXPL$
