-- Q978: International Tax [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["21% flat rate applied uniformly to all accumulated foreign earnings","15.5% on cash and cash-equivalent positions, and 8% on illiquid non-cash assets","10% flat rate with an 8-year installment payment election available","35% pre-TCJA corporate rate applied to all previously untaxed CFC earnings"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 965, the TCJA transition tax imposed a one-time repatriation charge on accumulated post-1986 deferred foreign earnings. Cash and cash-equivalent positions were taxed at 15.5%, while illiquid non-cash assets were taxed at 8%. Taxpayers could elect installment payments over eight years under Section 965(h).
Wrong (A): The 21% rate is the ongoing corporate income tax rate under the TCJA, not the transition tax rate for accumulated foreign earnings.
Wrong (C): The 10% rate is the deemed tangible income return rate under GILTI (Section 951A), not the Section 965 transition tax rate.
Wrong (D): The 35% pre-TCJA corporate rate was not applied to the transition tax; Congress enacted the reduced rates specifically for this one-time provision.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 978;

-- Q983: Owner-Entity Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The shareholder receives a distribution of at least $10,000 in the redemption transaction","It is substantially disproportionate, a complete termination, or not essentially equivalent to a dividend","The redeeming corporation has no current or accumulated earnings and profits at the time of redemption","The shareholder held the redeemed stock for more than one year before the redemption date"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 302(b), a stock redemption receives sale or exchange treatment if it meets one of four tests: (1) not essentially equivalent to a dividend under Sec. 302(b)(1), (2) substantially disproportionate under Sec. 302(b)(2), (3) complete termination of interest under Sec. 302(b)(3), or (4) partial liquidation for noncorporate shareholders under Sec. 302(b)(4).
Wrong (A): There is no minimum dollar threshold for sale or exchange treatment; the tests focus on the shareholder''s proportionate interest, not the amount received.
Wrong (C): E&P determines whether a distribution is a dividend if redemption treatment fails, but does not determine whether the redemption qualifies as a sale or exchange.
