-- Q993: Owner-Entity Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Tax-free return of basis for $35,000, with the $15,000 excess treated as capital gain","The entire $50,000 is taxable as dividend income to the shareholder","The entire $50,000 distribution is received tax-free as a return of capital","The $15,000 excess over basis is treated as ordinary income, not capital gain"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1368(b), distributions from an S corporation with no accumulated E&P are tax-free to the extent of stock basis. The first $35,000 reduces basis to zero as a nontaxable return of capital. The $15,000 excess is treated as gain from sale or exchange of stock under Sec. 1368(b)(2), taxed as capital gain.
