-- Q1017: Trusts and Estates [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Investment advisory fees paid for managing the trust''s portfolio assets","Tax preparation fees incurred for filing the trust''s fiduciary income tax return","Costs that would not have been incurred if the property were not held in a trust","Accounting fees for preparing the individual beneficiaries'' personal tax returns"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 67(e) and the Supreme Court''s Knight v. Commissioner decision, trust expenses that would not have been incurred if the property were not held in trust (e.g., trustee fees, fiduciary accountings) are fully deductible without regard to the 2% floor on miscellaneous itemized deductions.
Wrong (A): Investment advisory fees are commonly incurred by individuals, so they do not meet the ''would not have been incurred'' test and are subject to the 2% floor.
Wrong (B): Tax preparation fees can be incurred by individuals for their own returns, so they do not automatically qualify under the Section 67(e) standard.
Wrong (D): Accounting fees for personal tax returns are not trust-specific expenses at all and would not be deductible by the trust.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1017;

