-- Q1234: Capital Structure Tax Planning [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Yes, because RedCorp independently has less than $30 million in average annual gross receipts","No, because controlled group members are aggregated and the combined $50 million exceeds the threshold","Yes, because each controlled group member tests the gross receipts threshold on a separate-entity basis","No, because controlled group members are permanently prohibited from deducting any business interest expense"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Sections 163(j)(3) and 448(c)(2), all members of a controlled group are treated as a single employer for the gross receipts test. BlueCorp ($40M) and RedCorp ($10M) have combined average receipts of $50 million, exceeding the $30 million threshold, so neither qualifies for the small business exception.
Wrong (A): RedCorp cannot test the threshold independently; the aggregation rules under Section 448(c)(2) require combining all controlled group members.
Wrong (C): Separate-entity testing does not apply; the statute explicitly requires aggregation for controlled and affiliated groups.
Wrong (D): Controlled group members may deduct interest expense; the limitation under Section 163(j) is 30% of ATI, not a complete prohibition.$EXPL$
